# Build-context exclusions for the vendored shell.
#
# THIS FILE MUST LIVE HERE, not at the repo root. Docker reads the
# `.dockerignore` at the BUILD CONTEXT root, and this image's context is
# `./vendor/coinexchange/05_Web_Front` (see docker-compose.apps.yml). The root
# `.dockerignore` — which does exclude `node_modules` and `dist` — is never
# consulted for this build, so its protection did not extend here.
#
# What that cost: `COPY . .` copied the HOST's `node_modules` straight over the
# clean `npm install` the image had just done from the lockfile. That is the
# exact "works on my machine, baked into an image" hazard the root file was
# written to prevent, and it is worse here than usual because this tree is a
# 2017 dependency graph installed with --legacy-peer-deps: whatever a developer
# happens to have resolved locally would silently become the shipped bundle.
#
# It also masked a real build failure for a while, by making the container's own
# install irrelevant.
node_modules
dist

# Build output and local noise that must never reach the image.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
*.local

# The image builds from the lockfile; a host .env would leak into it.
.env
.env.*
